# Adopting agent-repo-kit — selective merge only (owner 2026-10-10)

The org's common agent layer lives in [agent-repo-kit](https://github.com/sumitbd/agent-repo-kit).
A repo takes it by **merging only the pieces it needs** into its own rules — never by running the
kit's `install.sh` or `kit-sync.sh --apply` over a repo that already has project rules (they
overwrite `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.cursor/rules/`, `.claude/settings.json`).

1. Diff the kit template against the repo; take the process rules, agents and skills the project
   will use. Skip what conflicts with org rules (org rules win) or with the repo's stack.
2. Merge chosen rules into the repo's `AGENTS.md` under "Org process rules (merged from
   agent-repo-kit)"; copy chosen `.claude/agents/` and `.claude/skills/` as-is.
3. Record the kit commit and what was taken in `.kit/kit.json` (`$comment`), so
   `sync-consumers.py` tracks the repo without overwriting project files.
4. Kit moves on → run the report, merge by hand what applies. Generic improvements found in a
   product go **upstream to the kit by PR**, never only into one repo.

Full text and reference adoption: hub `AGENTS.md` § "Adopting agent-repo-kit".
